model {
  extend basalt.build {
    metadata {
      constraint "Upstream sync evidence binds an exact repository commit, validated carry bytes and whole-filename order. Strict replay stops at the first failed carry and retains its failure and unattempted suffix before removing disposable source state. Replay never resets its input checkout or treats a diagnostic conflict resolution as a complete candidate. A new-pin retirement preserves the old-pin rollback carry and archives its patch and registry bytes and digests. Retirement requires exact-prefix equivalence and final affected runtime scenarios; any observed difference restores the carry. Dashboard batch profiling switches only the prepared middleware layer and restores its exact bytes after failure. The profiler does not depend on a retired carry file and refuses to overwrite source changed during the measurement. CI input and inherited-test inventories bind the pinned upstream tree; declarations follow the real replacement modules without dropping scenario coverage. Native declaration and credential-free Worker build fixtures supply release-marker command inputs without running migrations. Embedded MCP renderer bytes and content-hashed paths are regenerated together from the complete prepared cutover source with pinned Bun. Selection and aggregate proof follows Basalt's root workflow and declarations; upstream's unused CI selector is not the fork's execution authority. Cutover caller and credential scenarios use the declared CI jobs; attached Cloud requirements remain explicit manual coverage. Each changed exception is reviewed against its actual source and plan while unaffected fingerprints stay unchanged. Direct catalog publishers and their replayable overlays pin the served framework; frozen external snapshots stay unchanged, and pin updates preserve the already reviewed served app and UI bytes. A manual compiler-acceptance label starts only the exact ready cutover PR head, with event, live PR and base revalidation before provisioning. Acceptance uses isolated preview data and caches; failed catalog compilation, source binding, native smoke or teardown prevents a cutover receipt. Normal release previews retain their original receipt and trigger behavior."
    }
  }
}
